{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"e8b92dfa61801286ec37b29d3e7ae888c9307bbd0f564732532abfb95293f8a6","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_2e6c72d1d23bd3ceb7160953ab6a7673c56e12a18c5d8db3b94d036f4137a223","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a clear conceptual framework for Generalized Probability Kernels (GPK) but suffers from significant clarity issues in its mathematical exposition and writing. The notation is inconsistent, particularly regarding the use of indices and the definition of the mapping function phi, which hinders the reader's ability to follow the derivations. Additionally, the text contains numerous typos and grammatical errors that detract from the professional quality of the submission. While the logical flow from MMD to GPK is generally understandable, the lack of precise definitions and the presence of unexplained symbols in key theorems make the paper difficult to reproduce or verify without significant effort.","paper_id":"DigrnXQNMTe","paper_identity_sha256":"37a8f3ae4a736da82f8703f3966a1a91c4928fd34ef698a0e356a29853b6a7a3","prompt_identity_sha256":"4b1d485b8ac3e511a810bba037f196b30ba5ec05e37a4fe91b7bebc04a3b6872","raw_response_sha256":"e2b55955e050c0fd02d014fd014f26fea2ea34bcfbc5526fce8d80e0e354df05","request_identity_sha256":"07aa274027756e7ba105b340b25b247ed40d0ebb0073a2f29383bf4ccce7e2ab","reviewer_identity_sha256":"32b29c26fbf1508e066dfb25b1a9a3fe0654c5869a7da3020e1e8e61940befe3","role":"CLAR","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"c584f2ad45a9df71bdf0634323684c3a6fb4c3b98cdbcc677e29281a5189db29","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-002","SRC-005","SRC-012","SRC-016","SRC-021"],"review_text":"The writing quality is compromised by frequent typos and grammatical errors that distract from the technical content. For instance, the introduction contains the misspelling 'descrepancy' and the phrase 'underline distributions' which is likely a typo for 'underlying distributions' (SRC-002). Section 4.2 contains the typo 'memebers' (SRC-012), and Section 4.3 contains 'memethers' (SRC-016). Furthermore, the section numbering and cross-referencing are inconsistent; Section 5 refers to 'In section 2, we have introduced GPK family' (SRC-021), but the GPK framework is actually introduced in Section 4, while Section 2 is titled 'OUR CONTRIBUTIONS'. This misdirection confuses the reader regarding the paper's structure. The prose is often informal, using exclamation marks and conversational phrasing (e.g., 'We do not consider all other distributions in F that is irrelevant to our samples!') which is inappropriate for a formal research paper. These issues collectively reduce the clarity and professionalism of the exposition.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-WRT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-005","SRC-006","SRC-011","SRC-015","SRC-026"],"review_text":"The mathematical notation is inconsistent and often undefined, making it difficult to follow the derivations. In Section 3, the notation defines [k] as the set of discrete values, but in Definition 2 (SRC-011), the family S is defined on labels {y_1, ..., y_n} and the kernel maps from R^n x R^n, introducing a new dimension n that is not clearly distinguished from the support size k used elsewhere. This creates ambiguity about the dimensionality of the distributions. In Definition 4 (SRC-015), the plugin-estimator uses sample sizes n_1, n_2, m_1, m_2, but the text states 'n_1, n_2, m_1, m_2 denotes different i.i.d samples', conflating the sample size (a scalar) with the sample itself (a set). Furthermore, in the proof of Theorem 6 (SRC-026), the mapping function phi is defined using the notation '//' for element-wise division, but the text states 'where * means element-wise division', creating a direct contradiction between the symbol used in the equation and the symbol defined in the text. These inconsistencies prevent a clear understanding of the mathematical objects being manipulated.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-NOT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-021","SRC-031"],"review_text":"The paper includes several image references (e.g., SRC-021, SRC-031) that appear to be placeholders or broken links in the provided text, such as '![](images/...jpg)'. There are no machine-readable tables or detailed figure captions provided in the text to describe the content of these images. Consequently, it is impossible to evaluate the clarity or utility of the visual aids based on the available text. The absence of descriptive captions or alternative text for these figures means the reader cannot understand what the figures illustrate without access to the visual pixels, which are not part of this text-based review. The text does not provide any explicit textual descriptions of the visual content that would allow for an assessment of their clarity or relevance to the arguments made in the paper.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-FIG"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"5e20d7c374b1483d893f6f22d019d853a58d154d4ebcc27a05e929437d0c5cc6","paper_id":"DigrnXQNMTe","paper_ordinal":107,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"e2b55955e050c0fd02d014fd014f26fea2ea34bcfbc5526fce8d80e0e354df05","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"DigrnXQNMTe","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"d46a50b6923e4d4c268523fb572741c11fe59a1e69dd1cc1e8003f1922b85e9d","request_identity_sha256":"07aa274027756e7ba105b340b25b247ed40d0ebb0073a2f29383bf4ccce7e2ab","role":"CLAR","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v6","usage":{"completion_tokens":1045,"prompt_tokens":18663,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":19708},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"07aa274027756e7ba105b340b25b247ed40d0ebb0073a2f29383bf4ccce7e2ab","role":"CLAR","role_ordinal":1,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}